The task's prior note records a strict-interior-to-4 operation, but applying it indiscriminately was wrong here. In the test, background is 1 and frame-like structures are color 7. The first prediction filled all candidate cavities and was rejected; after one demo, a second prediction still filled too many regions and was also rejected. The demo had 9 background, a 0 frame/object pattern, and changed only some enclosed areas to 4; notably many line/frame structures remained unchanged. This establishes selection, not universal filling.

